module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.nested_pattern_accepted_by_the_interpreter_and_broken_in_emitted_rust

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data nested_pattern_accepted_by_the_interpreter_and_broken_in_emitted_rust: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "nested_pattern_accepted_by_the_interpreter_and_broken_in_emitted_rust" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a match that the seed's typecheck and interpreter accept, and whose emitted Rust either does not compile or panics. Two shapes, both found by the EdgeLabel cut (quiet-koi-814, gunbc#12799) only when neat-boar-16 ran self-host on srv1 -- no local claim, compile or interpreter run showed either. (1) A RECORD PATTERN that destructures a coproduct field -- `Edge { label: Authored { name: f }, target: t }` beside `Edge { label: Positional, target: _ }` -- is not checked for exhaustiveness over the field's coproduct, so adding an EdgeLabel arm left two such matches (`v2.extdeps.languages.dag` `dag_int_literal_magnitude_edge_target_optional` and its twin in `v2.std.compilers.target_model`) accepted and the emitted crate failed rustc E0004. The same blind spot covers a match whose scrutinee reaches the checker through a generic call (`list_at_optional`), which surfaced as six runtime pattern-match failures in the interpreter. (2) A THREE-LEVEL CONSTANT PATTERN -- `StructuralLabel { label: CoreMarker { marker: ArrowBodyEdge } }` beside a sibling arm with a different constant marker AND a wildcard sibling at the middle level (`StructuralLabel { label: _ }`) -- is lowered by `v1.compiler.emit_rust` as a guard on the middle variant only plus a `let ... else { unreachable!() }` on the innermost constant, so the first arm with the right middle variant but the wrong marker panics (`v2.std.node` `arrow_signature_edges_conform`, emitted line 676, in the self-host binary and the census driver). The interpreter evaluates both shapes correctly.",
    "HARM: the self-host route and every emitted consumer fail where every interpreter-side check is green, so the defect is found by the most expensive run and after review; shape (2) is a panic in a compiler binary, not a typed refusal.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the floor on the emitted path for shape (2) (an accepted program that panics), rung 1 for shape (1) (rustc refuses the emitted crate, loudly but late). The interpreter path is correct for both. CEILING: structurally guaranteed -- exhaustiveness over nested and record patterns is decidable, and a constant nested pattern has a total lowering (a nested match, not a guard plus let-else).",
    "SHAPE (2) CLIMBED, RUNG NOW 2 ON THE EMITTED PATH (mechanically preventable). WHY THE WILDCARD SIBLING SELECTED THE GUARD: `v1.compiler.emit_rust` `rc_grouped_arm_plan` planned an arm with no Rc-bound field (`O { mid: _ }`) as ungroupable, and `rc_group_representative` refuses the nested match for a whole outer variant when any one of its arms is ungroupable -- so one wildcard sibling pushed every arm of the variant onto the #8570 guard, whose `matches!` names only the middle variant while its prelude destructures the innermost constant with let-else. The fix is at that boundary, not a special case: an arm whose fields are all irrefutable IS the nested match's `_` arm, so it now plans as a wildcard member (no discriminated field, inner pattern `_`) and joins the group as its LAST member, under the same plain-binding subset rule as every other member. `test.claim.emit.nested_constant_pattern_emission_witness_test` `the_emitter_lowers_a_nested_constant_with_a_wildcard_sibling_as_a_nested_match` is the discriminating control: green with the fix, red with the regenerated emitter mirror reverted. It is rung 2, not 3: the guard lowering itself still omits nested constants below its first level, so an arm that stays ungrouped for another reason -- an authored guard, a string guard, two Rc-bound fields, a wildcard sibling that is not last -- still reaches the partial guard. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: every accepted refutable nested pattern lowers totally -- either the general decision-tree lowering `rc_grouped_match_arm_strs` names as its own next rung, or a guard that tests every refutable level -- so no accepted pattern lowers to unreachable!(). SHAPE (1) IS UNCHANGED: its trigger remains that the seed's match exhaustiveness check descends into record-pattern fields and through generic-call scrutinees, so an incomplete coproduct match refuses at typecheck.",
    "SHAPE (2) CLIMBED TO RUNG 3 ON THE EMITTED PATH (structurally guaranteed): every accepted refutable nested pattern now lowers totally. RE-DERIVED (DESIGN section 6b), THE EARLIEST UNJUSTIFIED BOUNDARY WAS THE GUARD, NOT THE GROUPING: the #8570 lowering is a guard plus a prelude, two renderings of one source pattern -- `v1.compiler.emit_rust` `rc_pattern_preludes` destructured an Rc-bound field with its full pattern under `let ... else { unreachable!() }`, while `collect_pattern_rc_variant_guards` tested only the field's outermost variant shape whenever no deeper Rc level needed a guard of its own. The let-else was sound only if the guard selected exactly what it destructured, and nothing established that. The grouped nested match (#8570's E0004 remedy, #12828's wildcard member) is an exhaustiveness rendering for the arms that fit it; it was never what made an arm's selection correct, so widening it to cover more arm kinds would have been a fifth special case over a guard that stayed partial. Both now read one rendering, `rc_field_pattern_str`, and the guard is `rc_field_selection_test`: the field's full pattern (binds erased, `match_pattern_binds_erased`), the string literals inside it, and recursively the same test for each deeper Rc-bound field -- so the let-else is unreachable by construction for every arm that reaches it, grouped or not. Two loud defects of the same arm kinds fell with it: a named string-literal field rendered as `ref __pos_..._val` with no field name (E0026, in both `emit_variant_pattern` and its Rc-aware twin), and a string literal inside an Rc-bound field was tested by the OUTER guard through a name bound only inside the field (E0425); `collect_pattern_string_guards_outside` now leaves those to the field's own test. EVIDENCE: a differential per arm kind (seed interpreter vs the emitted binary, same inputs) -- authored guard, string beside the Rc field, two Rc-bound fields, string inside the Rc field, top-level wildcard -- was red before (PANIC, PANIC, PANIC, E0026, E0425) and agrees after; `test.claim.emit.nested_constant_pattern_emission_witness_test` enrolls one interpreter claim per arm kind and one emitted-guard claim per arm kind as the permanent controls (each forbids the middle-variant-only guard). The authored-guard differential first required the interpreter to honor guards at all: gunbc.recurring_failure_mode interpreter_ignores_match_arm_guards. RESIDUE, A DIFFERENT INVALID STATE: a wildcard sibling that is not last makes every later arm of its variant dead source; the seed accepts the dead arm and the emitted crate refuses it under deny(unreachable_patterns), loudly, before and after this change -- rung 1 on the emitted path, trigger: the seed's match check refuses an arm no value can reach. SHAPE (1) IS UNCHANGED.",
    "THIRD SHAPE (N7-1, gunbc#13028): a binder taken from a payload field TWO variant levels down and passed straight into a constructor of the inner variant. Minimal reproducer, accepted by the seed typecheck and interpreter: `fn p(o: Optional<Outcome<A>>) -> Outcome<Int> { match o { Present { value: Accepted { value: a, diagnostics: d } } => Accepted { value: a.node, diagnostics: d }  Present { value: Rejected { diagnostics: r } } => Rejected { diagnostics: r }  Absent => Accepted { value: 0, diagnostics: None } } }`. In the emitted crate `d` is bound at its BOXED storage type and the constructor re-boxes it, `Box::new(d.clone())`, so rustc refuses E0308 (expected `Option<Rc<NonEmptyDiagnostics>>`, found `Box<Option<Rc<NonEmptyDiagnostics>>>`). It reached the native route as the emitted v2.compiler.resolve failing to build (EmittedCompilerBuildFailed), from a construct-tag caller of try_resolve_qualified_name_node; #13028 replaced that site with the one-level resolved_atom_node helper, which binds `d` at its value type -- an avoidance of this class, not a repair of it. WHY NO WITNESS IS ENROLLED FOR IT YET: the only emit witness helper, compile_dag_rust_emit_check, matches emitted TEXT, and the one-level form emits the SAME `Box::new(d.clone())` token and compiles (there `d` is the unboxed value); a text check cannot tell the two apart, so a probe written with it would be a decoration. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: an emit witness that BUILDS the emitted probe with rustc, sufficient for the nested form above to be a discriminating red and the one-level form its accepted control; then the lowering binds a nested payload binder at its value type.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.emit.nested_constant_pattern_emission_witness_test", decl_name: "the_interpreter_selects_each_nested_constant_arm", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.emit.nested_constant_pattern_emission_witness_test", decl_name: "the_emitter_lowers_a_nested_constant_with_a_wildcard_sibling_as_a_nested_match", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.emit.nested_constant_pattern_emission_witness_test", decl_name: "the_interpreter_selects_each_ungrouped_nested_arm", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.emit.nested_constant_pattern_emission_witness_test", decl_name: "the_emitter_guards_every_level_under_an_authored_guard", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.emit.nested_constant_pattern_emission_witness_test", decl_name: "the_emitter_guards_every_level_under_a_string_literal_beside_the_rc_field", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.emit.nested_constant_pattern_emission_witness_test", decl_name: "the_emitter_guards_every_level_under_two_rc_bound_fields", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.emit.nested_constant_pattern_emission_witness_test", decl_name: "the_emitter_guards_every_level_under_a_string_literal_inside_the_rc_field", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.emit.nested_constant_pattern_emission_witness_test", decl_name: "the_emitter_guards_every_level_under_a_top_level_wildcard", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
